-- map.iron -- Map[K: Hashable, V]: hash-based key/value container (Phase 33 STDLIB-03)
-- Phase 33 OQ-01 / GA1: this surface declares the generic Hashable BOUND on the
-- key parameter so the constraint enforcement in src/analyzer/typecheck.c
-- (check_generic_constraints, E0206) bites at every `Map[K, V]` instantiation:
-- `Map[String, Int]` / `Map[Int, V]` are well-formed (Int/String satisfy
-- Hashable via the primitive carve-out), while `Map[NonHashable, V]` is a
-- compile error naming the unsatisfied bound.
--
-- SCOPE (Plan 33-02): this plan declares the TYPE + the Hashable bound only —
-- enough for the OQ-01 constraint check to fire positively and negatively on
-- the check path. The full method surface (Map.new / set / get / has / remove /
-- len + the drop/copy element-lifecycle protocol over the IRON_MAP_IMPL backing
-- in src/runtime/iron_runtime.h) is the Wave-4 container rewrite (STDLIB-03
-- proper) and is intentionally NOT declared here — adding it now would pull in
-- the method-level-generic dispatch gap (OQ-02) tracked separately.
--
-- The hash-based backing (Iron_Map_<K>_<V>, name-mangled per
-- src/runtime/iron_runtime.h:982) is preserved and unchanged by this plan; the
-- runtime hashes the built-in Hashable primitives natively.
--
-- `val inner` opaque storage (not `var`) so v3.0 E0264 (mutable-field-needs-init)
-- does not fire on the stdlib surface — mirrors arena.iron / box.iron.

object Map[K: Hashable, V] {
    val inner: Int  -- opaque storage; the C runtime holds the real Iron_Map_<K>_<V>
}
